---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Mark from '~/components/sigmaflo/Mark.astro';

const SECURITY_EMAIL = 'security@sigmaflo.ai';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Security',
  description:
    'How Sigmaflo protects your financial data: deployment options, encryption, access controls, AI safeguards and answers to common security review questions.',
};

const commitments = [
  {
    lead: 'Zero trust architecture.',
    text: 'No user, device or network is trusted by default. Every access is tied to a named identity with multi-factor authentication, limited to what the role needs, and reviewed quarterly. There is no office network or VPN that grants access on its own.',
  },
  {
    lead: 'Data privacy & confidentiality.',
    text: 'We use it to deliver and support your service. It is never sold, shared or used for marketing.',
  },
  {
    lead: 'Deterministic & Rule-based core.',
    text: 'Every reported number comes from deterministic code you can inspect and re-run. A model can suggest a mapping or draft commentary but never to calculate a number or create a rule.',
  },
  {
    lead: 'Your data never trains a model.',
    text: "Not ours, not a provider's, and not to improve results for another customer. The mappings and rules built from your data stay with you.",
  },
  {
    lead: 'Data and Dual Access Controls.',
    text: 'Use our hosted service, or run Sigmaflo inside your own cloud account or infrastructure, where your data stays under your own controls.',
  },
];

const faqGroups = [
  {
    id: 'faq-data',
    title: 'Deployment and data',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'Where is our data hosted?',
        a: 'The hosted service runs on Google Cloud in the United States. Sigmaflo processes your data on your instructions, under a data processing agreement. If your data needs to stay in your own environment, see the customer-hosted option below.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Can we run Sigmaflo in our own environment instead?',
        a: "Yes. We offer a customer-hosted deployment that runs inside your own cloud account or on-premises infrastructure. Your data stays there, under your storage, network, logging and key management, and Sigmaflo doesn't keep a copy. If support ever needs access, you grant it to a named person for a set period.",
      },
      {
        q: 'Is our data encrypted?',
        a: 'Yes. Every connection uses TLS 1.2 or higher. In the hosted service, data at rest is encrypted with AES-256, with keys managed by Google Cloud Key Management Service. In a customer-hosted deployment, your own storage encryption and key management apply.',
      },
      {
        q: 'How does Sigmaflo connect to our ERP?',
        a: 'Through a read-only connection to your ERP or data warehouse, and we ingest only the fields statement preparation needs. Sigmaflo never writes back to your ledger. For customer-hosted deployments, we also document the minimum permissions and outbound connections the software needs, and you decide when to apply each update.',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'faq-ai',
    title: 'AI and models',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'Can a model change a number in our financials?',
        a: 'No. Every reported figure is produced by deterministic code: ingestion, tie-outs, matching, allocations and statement assembly. A model can propose a mapping or classification, or draft commentary, and that proposal takes effect only when a person accepts it. The acceptance is recorded with the run. Integrity checks such as balancing and rollforward integrity run separately and fail a run regardless of what any narrative says.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Where does model inference run, and what does it see?',
        a: "In the hosted service, on Google Cloud's Vertex AI, within our Google Cloud environment. Prompts never go to a consumer AI service. In a customer-hosted deployment, inference runs through the model service in your own cloud account, under your own cloud agreement. A model sees only what a task needs: the specific exception, the accounts and amounts involved, and the business context. Complete ledgers and trial balances aren't sent to a model as a matter of course.",
      },
      {
        q: 'Is our data used to train models?',
        a: "Never. We don't use your financial data to train a model, to improve results for another customer, or share it with a model provider under consumer terms.",
      },
      {
        q: 'How do you handle prompt injection?',
        a: "A vendor name or memo field can carry text written to manipulate an agent. That's why there is no path from model output to a financial figure: a model can't write a journal entry, change an amount or approve anything. Model-written text is labeled as such and reviewed by a person before it's accepted.",
      },
      {
        q: 'Can we run Sigmaflo with no third-party model at all?',
        a: "Yes. Tell us, and we'll scope an engagement with model features turned off. The deterministic work, from source entries through to the statement, still runs.",
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'faq-access',
    title: 'Access and people',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'Who at Sigmaflo can access our data?',
        a: 'Only people who need it to deliver or support your service, in three roles: the founder, engineering, and an accounting specialist who checks outputs for accounting correctness. Access goes to named people on documented approval, with no shared accounts, and is reviewed quarterly. Administrative actions are recorded in Google Cloud audit logs. In a customer-hosted deployment, no one at Sigmaflo has access unless you grant it. MFA is required on every account, with phishing-resistant methods for administrators.',
      },
      {
        q: 'How do you vet and train the people who work on Sigmaflo?',
        a: 'The same way for employees and contractors. Background screening comes before any access to production systems or customer data: identity and right-to-work, employment and education verification, and references, with criminal records checks where the law allows. Everyone signs confidentiality, acceptable use and IP agreements, and completes security training at onboarding and every year.',
      },
      {
        q: 'What do you require of laptops and devices?',
        a: 'Full-disk encryption, automatic screen lock, and a current operating system with security updates applied automatically. Removable media is never used for customer data. If a device is lost, we revoke its sessions and credentials and rotate anything it could have held. Contractors on their own equipment meet the same requirements and confirm them in writing.',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'faq-dev',
    title: 'Software and testing',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'How do you build the software securely?',
        a: 'Every change goes through a pull request and automated checks before it merges. Static analysis, dependency scanning and secret scanning run in the build. Critical findings are fixed within 7 days and high-severity findings within 30. Dependencies are pinned and reviewed before we adopt them. Development runs on synthetic data, never on copies of customer data.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Have you had a penetration test?',
        a: "Not yet. A third-party penetration test is planned, and annually after that, and we'll share the summary with customers. Code scan results are available under NDA. If you run Sigmaflo in your own environment, your team can test that deployment before it sees production data.",
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'faq-incidents',
    title: 'Incidents and continuity',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'How fast will you tell us about a security incident?',
        a: "Within 72 hours of becoming aware of an incident that affects or could affect you, including any compromise of our service, our software or the support access you've granted. We'll tell you what we know, what we're doing and what we recommend, and send a written report within 10 business days. We follow a documented incident response plan with defined severity levels and a single accountable owner.",
      },
      {
        q: "What happens if Sigmaflo isn't around?",
        a: "We're a small company, and key-person risk is real. Here's what limits it. Your source data stays in your ERP throughout. Your data, statements and audit trail export in open formats (CSV, XLSX, JSON) at any time, and we'll deliver any export within 5 business days of a request, including if you're leaving. The rules that produce your numbers are documented and inspectable. If continuity is a hard requirement, a customer-hosted deployment keeps running in your environment without us.",
      },
      {
        q: 'What support response times do you commit to?',
        a: '4 business hours for critical issues, 1 business day for high and 3 business days for normal. Availability targets for the hosted service are set in your order form. In a customer-hosted deployment, availability follows your own environment.',
      },
      {
        q: 'How do we report a vulnerability?',
        a: "Email security@sigmaflo.ai. We acknowledge within one business day and won't pursue researchers acting in good faith.",
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'faq-reviews',
    title: 'Vendors and reviews',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'Which subprocessors handle our data?',
        a: "In the hosted service, Google Cloud: infrastructure and Vertex AI model inference, in the United States. The tools we use to run our own company, such as Google Workspace and GitHub, don't receive your financial data. Every vendor is assessed before we use it and reviewed each year. Before adding a subprocessor that would handle your data, we give you at least 30 days' notice, and you can object. In a customer-hosted deployment, no subprocessor receives your data.",
      },
      {
        q: 'Do you hold SOC 2 or ISO 27001?',
        a: 'Not yet. A SOC 2 Type I examination is planned, and our controls are designed against the SOC 2 Trust Services Criteria and the NIST Cybersecurity Framework today. Google Cloud, where the hosted service runs, holds its own SOC 2 and ISO 27001 certifications.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Will you complete our security questionnaire?',
        a: "Yes. Under NDA we'll share our policy set and a detailed security overview, answer your questionnaire in full, sign your DPA, and join a call with your security team.",
      },
    ],
  },
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqGroups.flatMap((g) =>
    g.items.map((item) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: item.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: item.a },
    }))
  ),
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqJsonLd)} />
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="sf-hero" aria-labelledby="security-title">
    <div class="sf-container sf-hero-inner sf-hero-page">
      <p class="sf-label"><Mark />Security and compliance</p>
      <h1 id="security-title" class="sf-h1">How we keep your <span class="sf-accent">data safe.</span></h1>
      <p class="sf-lede sf-hero-lede">
        Sigmaflo is committed to ensuring the safety and confidentiality of your financial data. This page lists our
        policies and answers your biggest trust related questions.
      </p>
      <div class="sf-meta-row">
        <a href={`mailto:${SECURITY_EMAIL}`} class="sf-link">{SECURITY_EMAIL}</a>
        <span class="sf-meta-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <span>Last updated October 2026</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Commitments -->
  <section class="sf-band" aria-labelledby="commitments-title">
    <div class="sf-container sf-band-inner">
      <div class="sf-section-head" style="max-width: 820px; align-items: flex-start; text-align: left">
        <p class="sf-label"><Mark />Our principles</p>
        <h2 id="commitments-title" class="sf-h2">Our fundamental commitments.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="sf-commit-list">
        {
          commitments.map((c, i) => (
            <li>
              <span class="sf-commit-num" aria-hidden="true">
                {i + 1}
              </span>
              <p>
                <strong>{c.lead}</strong> {c.text}
              </p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="sf-container sf-section-inner sf-faq-section">
      <div class="sf-section-head" style="max-width: 820px">
        <p class="sf-label"><Mark />Security questions</p>
        <h2 id="faq-title" class="sf-h2">Your most frequently asked questions</h2>
        <p class="sf-lede">
          Short answers to the questions that come up in most vendor reviews. Your questionnaire gets full answers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="sf-faq-layout">
        <nav class="sf-faq-topics" aria-label="Question topics">
          <ul>
            {
              faqGroups.map((g) => (
                <li>
                  <a href={`#${g.id}`}>{g.title}</a>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
        </nav>

        <div class="sf-faq-groups">
          {
            faqGroups.map((g) => (
              <div class="sf-faq-group" id={g.id}>
                <h3 class="sf-faq-group-title">{g.title}</h3>
                <div class="sf-faq-list">
                  {g.items.map((item) => (
                    <details class="sf-faq-item">
                      <summary>
                        <span class="sf-faq-q">{item.q}</span>
                        <span class="sf-faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round">
                            <path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" />
                          </svg>
                        </span>
                      </summary>
                      <div class="sf-faq-answer">
                        <p>{item.a}</p>
                      </div>
                    </details>
                  ))}
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Closing box -->
  <section aria-labelledby="review-title">
    <div class="sf-container sf-cta-inner" style="padding-top: 0">
      <div class="sf-cta-panel">
        <h2 id="review-title" class="sf-h2">Running a vendor review?</h2>
        <p class="sf-lede">Send us your questionnaire, or ask for our policies under NDA.</p>
        <div class="sf-actions" style="padding-top: 0">
          <a href={`mailto:${SECURITY_EMAIL}`} class="btn btn-on-dark">Email {SECURITY_EMAIL}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
